                <pb facs="0326" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.51/571a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-03-30T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                                1920—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>97. Newspapers publish announcement apparently inspired, under Mexico City date
                    line, that Mexican Government intends to resume interest payments on foreign
                    debt. Date of resumption not stated.</p>
                <p>Ascertain if possible, and telegraph whether preferential treatment will be given
                    to coupons longest overdue, or if payments when begun will be applied to taking
                    up coupons currently maturing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
